=C2=A0=C2=A0-H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
=C2=A0=C2=A0-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
=C2=A0=C2=A0-d '{"model":"openai/gpt-4o-mini","messages":[{"role":"user","c=
ontent":"Hello"}]}'

=E2=80=83

What the response looks like. A standard OpenAI chat completion object. cho=
ices[0].message.content holds the text. usage has token counts. model shows=
 which model actually served the request, which matters when you use openro=
uter/auto and want to see what the router picked. If you already read OpenA=
I responses, you already know how to read these.

If the first call fails. A 401 is almost always the key header. A 402 means=
 the free-tier daily cap was hit or credits are needed for a paid model. A =
404 on a model string usually means dots vs hyphens; OpenRouter slugs use d=
ots, so claude-sonnet-4.6 not claude-sonnet-4-6. The models ( https://openr=
outer.ai/models?utm_source=3Demail&utm_medium=3Dlifecycle&utm_campaign=3Don=
boarding_v2&utm_content=3Db1_first_request&utm_campaign=3DOnboarding+Flow+-=
+v4+April+2026&utm_content=3DB1-1+First+Response&utm_medium=3Demail_action&=
utm_source=3Dcustomer.io ) page has every valid slug.

Free tier: 10 requests per day across 29 free models. No credit card to sta=
rt.

